    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To both parties. The route deviation is established but is not material, and the fare is recomputed accordingly. Measured on the figure that governs under POL-RD-01 — gps_trace.trace_distance_km of 17.57 km, not the trip record's rounded 17.6 km convenience copy — the excess over the platform optimal of 14.0 km is 3.57 km, or 25.5%. That clears both establishment tests (over 20% and over 0.8 km), so the deviation stands. It is below both materiality tests (50% and 8.0 km), so it is not material; the driver's point that no materiality consequence runs is accepted. POL-RD-06 is therefore not engaged, and no full-refund uplift or driver-conduct referral arises. Even if it were consulted, driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d of 1 against completed_trips_90d of 619 establishes no pattern, and the lifetime prior_deviation_flags counter may not be substituted for the 90-day figure. The driver's congestion excuse does not reduce the refund. The only traffic advisory in the bundle (EV-ADVIS-00107-01) carries a null payload — it names no road, has no validity window and no alternative-route distance — so under POL-RD-03 it exonerates nothing. Nor does it trigger escalation under POL-RD-10(5): the driver's statement cites no traffic_advisory at all, and an exculpatory clause invoked with nothing behind it is not an untested limb; his bare 'CTE very jam' assertion is discarded under POL-RD-08, which places the burden on the driver and requires a specific artifact and clause. Nothing shifts the excess to the rider. The two-message chat shows the rider asking why the driver exited at Whitely and the driver answering about the jam; there is no rider instruction and waypoint_hint is null on both messages, so POL-RD-04 does not run. There is no relocation (pickup_amended_at and dropoff_amended_at are null and amended_optimal_distance_km is null, so POL-RD-05 cannot run) and the vehicle is RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL (POL-RD-12 not engaged); the booked 14.0 km optimal is the sole baseline. The refund is arithmetic under POL-RD-02, the fare being METERED, with the 1.35 surge multiplier read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier (the trip record carries no such field): recomputed_fare = (3.80 + 0.75 x 14.0 + 0.28 x 24.0) x 1.35 + 0.80 = 29.177. charged_total is 36.60. Refund = 36.60 - 29.177 = 7.423, rounded up to SGD 7.45. That is 20.3% of the charge — above the SGD 0.50 de minimis floor and below the 90% full-refund line — so the outcome is a partial refund of SGD 7.45, not the SGD 12.00 claimed. The trace is clean for POL-RD-07 purposes (100% coverage, no gaps, max_gap_sec 0, a steady 10-second interval), so there is no impairment and no POL-RD-10(3) escalation. The rider's history (deviation_claims_60d of 5 and only 1 substantiated) triggers POL-RD-08's requirement of corroboration beyond the trace for an excess under 30%; that is met by the driver's own statement that he went by Newton and Kim Seng, which admits the off-optimal route, and in any event that factor may not be used to deny an otherwise proven claim. No escalation trigger fires. There is no off-route or phantom ERP line (tolls_erp 0.00, empty gantry list), so nothing is added or corrected under POL-RD-09 and no billing-integrity or other referral arises. No driver compensation is due: the billed distance (17.6 km) is not less than the trace distance, so the POL-RD-04 shortfall limb does not apply."
