er rather than being decided against the driver on a defence the record gives no one the means to test. What would resolve it: the complete LTA traffic advisory for the CTE southbound corridor near Chin Swee on the night of 18 July 2026; if it shows a qualifying event on the optimal corridor within a window overlapping the trip, POL-RD-03 may excuse part or all of the excess. For transparency, if the case were decided on the present record the arithmetic under POL-RD-02 (fare_model METERED) would be recomputed_fare = ((3.80 + 0.75 x 14.0 + 0.28 x 24.0) x 1.35) + 0.80 = 29.177, the 1.35 surge multiplier read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier, the only artifact that carries it; refund = charged_total 36.60 less 29.177 = 7.423, rounded up to SGD 7.45 — a PARTIAL_REFUND of $7.45, not the $12.00 claimed and not a full refund, and above the SGD 0.50 de minimis floor. No ERP or toll line arises (empty gantry list, tolls 0.00), so no POL-RD-09 pass-through or billing-integrity correction is due, and there is no distance-billing shortfall, so no POL-RD-04 driver compensation arises. The rider's additional corroboration requirement for a sub-30% excess (POL-RD-08, given 5 deviation claims and 1 substantiated in 60 days) is met by the driver's own counterparty statement admitting the route by Newton and Kim Seng — an independent source named in POL-RD-07(ii) — so the rider's claim is not denied on profile grounds."
